bic_trace_step.reason:
This commit introduces the vulnerable construct in `vcpu_block()`. Specifically, the lines:

+	if (is_guest_mode(vcpu)) {
+		if (kvm_check_nested_events(vcpu) < 0)
+			return 0;
+	}

propagate any negative error code (such as `-EBUSY` when there is an already-injected event) from `kvm_check_nested_events()` by returning `0` from `vcpu_block()`. This causes a spurious exit to userspace, which is the exact root cause of the vulnerability.
